        "description": "<figure>\n\n<img alt=\"A woman using SoundCloud to purchase music.\" data-caption=\"\" data-portal-copyright=\"Image: SoundCloud\" data-has-syndication-rights=\"1\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/6a8da72a57472ab559aad907_600400-1.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\" />\n\t<figcaption>\n\t\t</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">SoundCloud has launched a new beta feature that allows artists on the audio streaming platform to <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/playbook-articles/soundcloud-introduces-direct-music-purchases-with-zero-commission\">sell music directly</a> from their profiles, instead of diverting fans to purchase from third-party services like Bandcamp and Beatport. The feature aims to give listeners a better way to support the musicians behind their favorite songs, because SoundCloud isn't taking any commission from these sales - meaning everything goes directly to the artists.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">By comparis",
